+# Product Reserve API Scope
+
+## Feature
+
+Add an API to reserve product stock for the existing `catalog.Product` model.
+
+## Observable behavior
+
+- A client can request reservation of a positive quantity for one product.
+- If product stock is lower than the requested quantity, the API rejects the request with HTTP 409.
+- If stock is sufficient, the API subtracts the requested quantity from `Product.stock` and returns success.
+- The existing `Product` model is the target aggregate/root for this feature.
+
+## Boundaries
+
+- In scope: reservation command, stock invariant, HTTP endpoint, request validation, tests, migrations/checks if needed.
+- Out of scope: separate reservation records, expiration/release flow, user/account ownership, authentication, idempotency keys, payment/order integration, async/event delivery.
+
+## Pre-approved gate decisions
+
+- Bounded context placement: architect decides by standard ownership principle; default expectation is extending existing `catalog` because the invariant is Product stock.
+- Active design lenses: ddd, db, api.
+- API stack: choose the project-default minimal stack after inspecting existing dependencies.
+- Test runner: choose the project-default runner after inspecting existing configuration.
